# Reusable Components & Packages

- Prefer `@dripplex/ui` primitives and design tokens over local one-off components.
- Put cross-app types in `@dripplex/types`; never redefine the same enum/DTO shape in two apps.
- HTTP access goes through `@dripplex/sdk` — do not scatter raw `fetch` clients with duplicated auth headers.
- Shared React state/effects live in `@dripplex/hooks`.
- Pure helpers (money, dates, phone NG formats) live in `@dripplex/utils`.
- Tooling baselines come from `@dripplex/config` (TS / ESLint / Prettier). Extend; do not fork copies.
- If you need a new shared abstraction, add it to the correct package with exports, types, and tests — do not leave a private copy inside an app.
